{"at": "2026-07-13T00:10:32Z", "commit_ref": "none", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "output", "content": "Authored the full spec 0040 (steering .spec-md + 13-step .spec-jsonl) from the operator preliminary spec specs/0038/.manual/011-tree-chart-geometry-spec.md, grounding every pointer against the current post-0038 tree (Read-before-cite).\n\nFour independent Optical Constructor improvements, all editing existing files (no new module):\n\nPart A - Faceted tree UX (steps 1-3): alphabetical order at every level in Facets.buildTree (branch sort at Facets.fs:248) and both host tree assemblies (MaterialsWindowView.fs:719-760, LibraryWindowView.fs:844-898); collapsible tree with a new Handlers.toggleNode and collapsed-by-default persisted expansion (FacetedTreeControls.fs:149-167,:351-368); visible selection via a new State.selectedCode painted with chosenBackground (FacetedTreeControls.fs:173).\n\nPart B - Facet totality via seeds (steps 4-5): re-seed the three complexity=None coded presets - Silicon (MaterialLibrary.fs:376), Langasite (:384), Vacuum spacer (:440) - with complexity=Some value trees carrying anisotropy+transparency as data; drop the appliesTo gates on materialAnisotropyDef (LibraryFacets.fs:217-232) and materialTransparencyDef (:252-267), dispersive materials -> Absorbing. No runtime engine-tensor classifier.\n\nPart C - Chart applicability (steps 6-7): restrict gyrationChart (NkDispersionChart.fs:110-130) and muChart (:141-162) to the class's independent components, reusing gyrationComponents/gyrationComponentLabel/MuKind (MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:436-444,:421-428,:72-74); wrap the description TextBox.\n\nPart D - Sample geometry and R/T (steps 8-12): Plate-requires-substrate in validateSample (ElementId.fs:802-811); add Sample.supportedEmission reusing the Emission DU (Placement.fs:108-138), ThinFilm forced EmitReflectedOnly / Plate default EmitBoth; editor R/T checkboxes; bound the placed element's Emission and the experiment MeasurementMode (Experiments.fs:106-110); substrate Set... via the Materials Select window by adding a SampleSubstrateTarget to SelectionTarget (WindowMode.fs:31-33).\n\nStep 13 WIRE_UI: finalise composition and drive the ui-smoke surface (Materials, Library, Material editor, Sample editor) without throwing, gates at/above baseline.\n\nNotable correction vs the preliminary spec: gyrationChart/muChart line numbers were stale (preliminary cited :94-114/:125-146; actual :110-130/:141-162), and hasGyration/hasMagnetic live in NkDispersionChart.fs:171-180, not MaterialComplexityEditor.fs - the spec uses the verified current locations. Recorded interpretation (spec-md B.0/B.1): Part B totality is achieved by re-seeding the coded presets with complexity value trees (the preliminary's named mechanism), keeping properties = complexity.toProperties per the existing seed convention.\n"}
{"at": "2026-07-13T00:37:19Z", "commit_ref": "none", "intent": "spec", "actor": "user", "kind": "output", "content": "[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\Berreman\\\\OpticalConstructor\\\\OpticalConstructor.Ui\\\\SampleEditorView.fs\", \"offset\": 940, \"limit\": 55}\nI have thorough grounding on Parts A, C, and most of D. Let me nail the Part D.3 substrate-select mechanism and the Part B seed presets (`complexity = None` coded materials). Let me look at both in parallel.\n[tool Grep] {\"pattern\": \"SelectionTarget|SampleLayerTarget|SampleSubstrateTarget|chooseMaterialForLayer|onChooseMaterial|LayerPosition|SubstrateSlot|type SampleEditorContext|chooseMaterial\"...\n[tool Grep] {\"pattern\": \"complexity = None|complexity = Some|let builtInEntries|standardCategories|let materialDispersion|silicon|langasite|vacuum|spacer\", \"output_mode\": \"content\", \"glob\":...\nLet me read `materialDispersion` and the `MaterialComplexity` seed shape (Part B mechanism), plus find the `SelectionTarget` DU for Part D.3.\n[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\Berreman\\\\OpticalConstructor\\\\OpticalConstructor.Domain\\\\MaterialLibrary.fs\", \"offset\": 180, \"limit\": 50}\n[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\Berreman\\\\OpticalConstructor\\\\OpticalConstructor.Domain\\\\MaterialLibrary.fs\", \"offset\": 595, \"limit\": 40}\n[tool Grep] {\"pattern\": \"type SelectionTarget|SampleLayerTarget|type SelectionContext|type LibraryWindowMode|Select of\", \"output_mode\": \"content\", \"glob\": \"**/*.fs\", \"-n\": true}\n[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\Berreman\\\\OpticalConstructor\\\\OpticalConstructor.Domain\\\\WindowMode.fs\"}\nI have thorough grounding. Let me do a final confirming read of the `builtInEntries` seed block (central to Part B) and the seeded sample structures, so the re-seed directive is concrete.\n[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\Berreman\\\\OpticalConstructor\\\\OpticalConstructor.Domain\\\\MaterialLibrary.fs\", \"offset\": 368, \"limit\": 100}\nI now have complete, verified grounding across all four parts. Let me capture the key decision before authoring: for Part B, the three coded presets (silicon `MaterialLibrary.fs:376`, langasite `:384`, vacuum spacer `:440`) carry `complexity = None`, so I'll direct re-seeding them with `complexity = Some` value trees (the preliminary spec's named mechanism), reusing the existing `*.toProperties` seed convention. Now let me write the steering `.spec-md`.\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0040\\\\.spec-md\", \"content\": \"# Spec 0040 — Faceted tree UX, facet totality, chart applicability, and sample geometry / R–T\\n\\nFour in...\n[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0040\\\\.spec-md\"}\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0040\\\\.spec-md\", \"content\": \"# Spec 0040 — Faceted tree UX, facet totality, chart applicability, and sample geometry / R–T\\n\\nFour in...\nThe steering narrative is in place. Now the authoritative step list `.spec-jsonl` — 13 forward-only steps, all `IMPLEMENT` except the final `WIRE_UI`, each carrying verified pointers.\n[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0040\\\\.spec-jsonl\"}\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0040\\\\.spec-jsonl\", \"content\": \"{\\\"number\\\":1,\\\"anchor\\\":\\\"IMPLEMENT\\\",\\\"ac\\\":\\\"AC-A1\\\",\\\"touches\\\":[\\\"OpticalConstructor.Domain\\\",\\\"...\nLet me validate the JSONL is well-formed (valid JSON per line, contiguous numbering, valid anchors) before recording history.\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd C:/GitHub/Berreman && python -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nanchors={'ADD_COMPONENT','ADD_CONTRACT','IMPLEMENT','IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT','MERGE_CONTRACT','MODIFY_CONTRACT','REN...\nJSONL is structurally valid. Let me verify LF endings on both files (CLAUDE.md discipline) before recording history.\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd C:/GitHub/Berreman && python -c \\\"\\nfor f in ['specs/0040/.spec-md','specs/0040/.spec-jsonl']:\\n    b=open(f,'rb').read()\\n    print(f, 'CRLF' if b'\\\\r\\\\n' in b ...\nBoth files are LF-only and valid. Now I'll record the history entry via the project's safe writer. First the content payload file, then the CLI append.\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0040\\\\.artifacts\\\\0040-spec-author-output.txt\", \"content\": \"Authored the full spec 0040 (steering .spec-md + 13-step .spec-jsonl) fro...\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd C:/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator 2>/dev/null && python -m ai_strategy_generator.spec_writer.history_cli append \\\\\\n    --spec-folder \\\"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs...\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd C:/GitHub/Berreman && python -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nlines=open('specs/0040/.history',encoding='utf-8').read().splitlines()\\nprint('history lines:',len(lines))\\nfor ...\nDone. Spec 0040 is authored — both files plus the history entry are in place.\n\n## What I wrote\n\n**`specs/0040/.spec-md`** — the steering narrative: binding constraints (§0) and four Part sections (A–D) with verified `file:line` pointers, no step enumeration, no acceptance/files/tests sections (those live in the steps).\n\n**`specs/0040/.spec-jsonl`** — 13 forward-only steps, all `IMPLEMENT` except the final `WIRE_UI` (wires/verifies the composition root). Validated: contiguous numbering 1–13, valid anchors, no forward deps, LF endings.\n\n**`.history`** — appended one `spec / agent / output` row via the `history_cli` safe writer (now 2 lines).\n\n## The spec, by part (each an independently-green slice)\n\n- **Part A — faceted tree (steps 1–3):** alphabetical order at every level (`Facets.buildTree` branch sort at `Facets.fs:248` + both host projections); collapsible tree with a new `Handlers.toggleNode` and collapsed-by-default persisted expansion; visible selection via a new `State.selectedCode` painted with the existing `chosenBackground`.\n- **Part B — facet totality (steps 4–5):** re-seed the three `complexity = None` coded presets (Silicon/Langasite/Vacuum) with `complexity = Some` value trees so anisotropy/transparency are data; drop the two `appliesTo` gates; dispersive → Absorbing. No runtime tensor classifier.\n- **Part C — charts (steps 6–7):** restrict `gyrationChart`/`muChart` to each class's independent components (reusing `gyrationComponents`/`gyrationComponentLabel`/`MuKind`); wrap the description box.\n- **Part D — geometry & R/T (steps 8–12):** Plate-requires-substrate in `validateSample`; `Sample.supportedEmission` reusing the `Emission` DU (ThinFilm forced R-only, Plate default both); editor R/T checkboxes; bound the placed element + experiment `MeasurementMode`; substrate \"Set…\" via the Materials Select window (new `SampleSubstrateTarget`).\n\n## Two grounding notes worth flagging\n\n- The preliminary spec's line numbers for `gyrationChart`/`muChart` were **stale** (it cited `:94-114`/`:125-146`; actual `:110-130`/`:141-162`), and it located `hasGyration`/`hasMagnetic` in the wrong file. The spec uses the **verified current** locations.\n- I recorded the load-bearing interpretation in `.spec-md` §B.0/B.1: Part B totality is achieved by re-seeding the coded presets with `complexity` value trees (the preliminary's named mechanism), keeping `properties = complexity.toProperties` per the existing seed convention — this changes those presets' physics to their ladder expression, which is the operator's explicit \"re-seed\" intent.\n\nI can't run git here (the arc-runner owns commits), so nothing is committed — the files are staged in the spec folder for the next cycle.\nDone. Spec 0040 is authored — both files plus the history entry are in place.\n\n## What I wrote\n\n**`specs/0040/.spec-md`** — the steering narrative: binding constraints (§0) and four Part sections (A–D) with verified `file:line` pointers, no step enumeration, no acceptance/files/tests sections (those live in the steps).\n\n**`specs/0040/.spec-jsonl`** — 13 forward-only steps, all `IMPLEMENT` except the final `WIRE_UI` (wires/verifies the composition root). Validated: contiguous numbering 1–13, valid anchors, no forward deps, LF endings.\n\n**`.history`** — appended one `spec / agent / output` row via the `history_cli` safe writer (now 2 lines).\n\n## The spec, by part (each an independently-green slice)\n\n- **Part A — faceted tree (steps 1–3):** alphabetical order at every level (`Facets.buildTree` branch sort at `Facets.fs:248` + both host projections); collapsible tree with a new `Handlers.toggleNode` and collapsed-by-default persisted expansion; visible selection via a new `State.selectedCode` painted with the existing `chosenBackground`.\n- **Part B — facet totality (steps 4–5):** re-seed the three `complexity = None` coded presets (Silicon/Langasite/Vacuum) with `complexity = Some` value trees so anisotropy/transparency are data; drop the two `appliesTo` gates; dispersive → Absorbing. No runtime tensor classifier.\n- **Part C — charts (steps 6–7):** restrict `gyrationChart`/`muChart` to each class's independent components (reusing `gyrationComponents`/`gyrationComponentLabel`/`MuKind`); wrap the description box.\n- **Part D — geometry & R/T (steps 8–12):** Plate-requires-substrate in `validateSample`; `Sample.supportedEmission` reusing the `Emission` DU (ThinFilm forced R-only, Plate default both); editor R/T checkboxes; bound the placed element + experiment `MeasurementMode`; substrate \"Set…\" via the Materials Select window (new `SampleSubstrateTarget`).\n\n## Two grounding notes worth flagging\n\n- The preliminary spec's line numbers for `gyrationChart`/`muChart` were **stale** (it cited `:94-114`/`:125-146`; actual `:110-130`/`:141-162`), and it located `hasGyration`/`hasMagnetic` in the wrong file. The spec uses the **verified current** locations.\n- I recorded the load-bearing interpretation in `.spec-md` §B.0/B.1: Part B totality is achieved by re-seeding the coded presets with `complexity` value trees (the preliminary's named mechanism), keeping `properties = complexity.toProperties` per the existing seed convention — this changes those presets' physics to their ladder expression, which is the operator's explicit \"re-seed\" intent.\n\nI can't run git here (the arc-runner owns commits), so nothing is committed — the files are staged in the spec folder for the next cycle."}
