c-md (Parts A-D, all edits to existing OpticalC...\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd /c/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator && python -m ai_strategy_generator.spec_writer.history_cli append \\\\\\n    --spec-folder \\\"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0040\\\" \\\\\\...\nThe safe writer returned line offset `984`. Let me verify the appended `.history` line parses and is the correct decision entry.\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"python - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\nlines = open('specs/0040/.history', encoding='utf-8').read().splitlines()\\nprint('history total lines:', len(lines))\\nlast = json.load...\nAll three authoritative files are written and validated. The gates cycle is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI reconciled `specs/0040/.spec-md` (a four-part Optical Constructor spec, all edits to **existing** `OpticalConstructor.Domain / Controls / Ui / App` files — §0.1 adds no new file or module) against the `.gates/` tree.\n\n**Decision: `include` all five available gates. No exclusions, no `propose-new`.**\n\nThe existing gate menu already covers the spec's entire testable surface, and every step's `touches` lands in a test project one of these gates runs:\n\n| Gate | Why included |\n|------|--------------|\n| **build** | Green build non-negotiable (§0.2); every step edits `.fs` inside `Berreman.slnx`. |\n| **unit-tests** | Borderline (no pure-solver edit) but included per the default-inclusion bias — `applies_to` matches `Berreman/**/*.fs`, and Part B re-seeds `MaterialLibrary` through the shared dispersion ladder, so BerremanTests is cheap regression insurance. Flagged for the operator to exclude post-cycle if desired. |\n| **constructor-unit-tests** | Pure-Domain surface named in §0.3: `Facets.buildTree` sort, facet totality, `validateSample` / `supportedEmission` / `MeasurementMode.ofEmission` (steps 1–5, 8–9, 12). |\n| **ui-smoke** | Step 13 (WIRE_UI) requires headless render of the Materials/Library windows + Material/Sample editors over the new tree/chart/emission behaviour. |\n| **ui-tests** | Per-panel interaction: chevron toggle, visible selection, restricted gyration/μ charts, Plate R/T checkboxes, substrate Select flow (steps 2–3, 6, 10–11). |\n\nAll five are `filter: none`, so no `select` lists were emitted. No `propose-new` was warranted — there is no uncovered testable aspect (there's no dedicated `OpticalConstructor.Controls` test project; its logic is exercised through `OpticalConstructor.Tests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`), and no subsystem is removed that would justify an `exclude`.\n\n**Files written (within allowed scope only):**\n- `.gate-history` — 5 `include` rows (LF, valid JSONL).\n- `.spec-bundle` — `gates` array set to the five names; all other fields untouched, clean diff, no CRLF churn.\n- `.history` — one `gates / agent / decision` line appended via the `history_cli` safe writer (now 8 lines, valid JSONL).\n- `.artifacts/gates-decision-summary.txt` — the transient content payload the history append required.\n\nThe `.gate-history` was previously empty and there were no prior rejects or `.proposed-gates/` to consult.\nAll three authoritative files are written and validated. The gates cycle is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI reconciled `specs/0040/.spec-md` (a four-part Optical Constructor spec, all edits to **existing** `OpticalConstructor.Domain / Controls / Ui / App` files — §0.1 adds no new file or module) against the `.gates/` tree.\n\n**Decision: `include` all five available gates. No exclusions, no `propose-new`.**\n\nThe existing gate menu already covers the spec's entire testable surface, and every step's `touches` lands in a test project one of these gates runs:\n\n| Gate | Why included |\n|------|--------------|\n| **build** | Green build non-negotiable (§0.2); every step edits `.fs` inside `Berreman.slnx`. |\n| **unit-tests** | Borderline (no pure-solver edit) but included per the default-inclusion bias — `applies_to` matches `Berreman/**/*.fs`, and Part B re-seeds `MaterialLibrary` through the shared dispersion ladder, so BerremanTests is cheap regression insurance. Flagged for the operator to exclude post-cycle if desired. |\n| **constructor-unit-tests** | Pure-Domain surface named in §0.3: `Facets.buildTree` sort, facet totality, `validateSample` / `supportedEmission` / `MeasurementMode.ofEmission` (steps 1–5, 8–9, 12). |\n| **ui-smoke** | Step 13 (WIRE_UI) requires headless render of the Materials/Library windows + Material/Sample editors over the new tree/chart/emission behaviour. |\n| **ui-tests** | Per-panel interaction: chevron toggle, visible selection, restricted gyration/μ charts, Plate R/T checkboxes, substrate Select flow (steps 2–3, 6, 10–11). |\n\nAll five are `filter: none`, so no `select` lists were emitted. No `propose-new` was warranted — there is no uncovered testable aspect (there's no dedicated `OpticalConstructor.Controls` test project; its logic is exercised through `OpticalConstructor.Tests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`), and no subsystem is removed that would justify an `exclude`.\n\n**Files written (within allowed scope only):**\n- `.gate-history` — 5 `include` rows (LF, valid JSONL).\n- `.spec-bundle` — `gates` array set to the five names; all other fields untouched, clean diff, no CRLF churn.\n- `.history` — one `gates / agent / decision` line appended via the `history_cli` safe writer (now 8 lines, valid JSONL).\n- `.artifacts/gates-decision-summary.txt` — the transient content payload the history append required.\n\nThe `.gate-history` was previously empty and there were no prior rejects or `.proposed-gates/` to consult."}
